      R. Q. 2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَكْرُكُهُ</span></b> , (K,) relating to a skin [of
milk], (TA,) means <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَخُّضُهُ</span> [i. e. <i>Its being agitated</i>] <i>with the butter.</i> (K, TA. [In the CK,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَكْرَكَهُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَخَّضَهُ</span> are put for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَرَكْرُكُهُ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَخُّضُهُ</span>.])

